{"name":"Oxford by Night","hex":"#001b2e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oxford","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Oxford (cloth)","Alternative letter-case form of Oxford (shoe)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oxford"},{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"}],"entries":[{"title":"By Night","blocks":[{"text":"By Night is a Swedish metalcore band from Falkenberg, formed by André Gonzales (guitar), Simon Wien (guitar), and Per Qvarnström (drums) in 1999. After several line-up changes, bassist Henrik Persson joined and stayed, later on singer Christoffer Andersson as well. Two demos were recorded, By Night (2000) and Derelict (2001)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/By_Night","wikidata":"Q683668"},{"title":"Oxford","blocks":[{"text":"Oxford is a cathedral city and non-metropolitan district in Oxfordshire, England, of which it is the county town."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Museum_of_Oxford_%285652685943%29.jpg/330px-Museum_of_Oxford_%285652685943%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxford","wikidata":"Q34217"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Bridge_of_Sighs_with_Lampost%2C_Oxford%2C_July_25%2C_2023.jpg/500px-Bridge_of_Sighs_with_Lampost%2C_Oxford%2C_July_25%2C_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Bridge_of_Sighs_with_Lampost%2C_Oxford%2C_July_25%2C_2023.jpg/1280px-Bridge_of_Sighs_with_Lampost%2C_Oxford%2C_July_25%2C_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Bridge_of_Sighs_with_Lampost%2C_Oxford%2C_July_25%2C_2023.jpg/500px-Bridge_of_Sighs_with_Lampost%2C_Oxford%2C_July_25%2C_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABridge_of_Sighs_with_Lampost%2C_Oxford%2C_July_25%